pi-coding-agent 1.5.1 + Tron backports (declared by packages/gateway/pi-coding-agent-patch.json)

Apply with git apply at tag v1.5.1 (dd30101cfc5b0609411dd80b6f93adbc14db14cf).

1. projectDir. Upstream proposal commit 7a795da1c69cbc2df30485c173d14d2266ead2ba (parent a447ba1).
   A session can run in a subdirectory (cwd) while its project .pi comes from projectDir:
   settings, resources, packages, SYSTEM.md, and built-in MCP config, whose stdio servers
   start in projectDir. Tools, context files, .agents/skills discovery and session grouping
   keep cwd. Extensions read ctx.projectDir. projectDir defaults to cwd.

2. Idle systemPrompt keeps extension sections (Tron #1312). A before_agent_start handler sets
   systemPromptOptions.sections for its run (the built-in MCP extension's mcp_servers listing),
   and the transcript keeps a section until a later run stops setting it, but settlement dropped
   the run options so session.systemPrompt rendered only the base options between runs. Between
   runs it now adds the sections the transcript still gives the model that Pi does not render
   itself (buildIdleSystemPrompt). It is read-only: no section is written into base or run
   options, so a section set for one run is still removed by the next request's diff. A
   transcript section with a built-in name is left to the base options, which the next diff
   applies; a handler that overrides a built-in section therefore shows only during its run.

3. Revocable run start (Tron #1340). Pi 1.2 counts a run busy from _startRun, and calls a
   host's prompt preflightResult("started") after preparing it but outside the start's
   failure cleanup. A host that revokes the prepared prompt by throwing there (the Gateway
   does when Stop arrived during preflight compaction or before_agent_start) left the
   session streaming with no run, so abort() and waitForIdle() never settled. The callback
   now runs inside that cleanup: a throw ends the start like a failed preparation, the
   session is idle again, and the prompt is neither appended nor sent.

4. Config-read lifetime (Tron #2199). Registration refreshes load models.json
   asynchronously before downstream provider supersession. Serialize fresh config
   reads in admission order, so an older detached refresh cannot start store work
   after a newer awaited readiness pass. Independent targeted refreshes are retained.

5. Explicit pending loadout names (Tron #2181). Reapplying a saved selection may remove
   newly autoactivated direct tools before MCP servers register. When that narrows the
   loadout, preserve pending restored names explicitly requested by the same call, while
   discarding unrequested ones. Addition-only discovery updates still keep pending names.
   Upstream 1.4 auto-activation remains enabled; Tron still reapplies the recorded selection.

6. Bundled HTTP dependency (Tron #2470). Rebuild the child CLI and RPC entry with
   undici 8.12.4. Gateway overrides do not replace their inlined dependency. The SDK
   checker executes both actual child entries against a loopback integrity-mismatch response.

